@page
@model FitAdvisor.Pages.CaloriePlanModel

<h2>Historical Calorie Plan Comparison</h2>

<p>These historical outputs contain a known double-deficit defect: they assume age 30 and activity multiplier 1.5, then apply two successive 20% reductions with intermediate truncation. They are shown for comparison, not as corrected recommendations. The meal diary has a separate historical target. <a asp-page="/NutritionCalculator">Calculate with explicit inputs</a>.</p>
<p>Body fat values are approximate BMI-based estimates, not precise medical measurements. Target body fat is a hypothetical estimate at your target weight.</p>
@if (Model.CalculationError != null)
{
    <p class="text-danger">@Model.CalculationError</p>
}
else
{
    <p><strong>Current Weight:</strong> @Model.Weight kg</p>
    <p><strong>Target Weight:</strong> @Model.TargetWeight kg</p>
    <p><strong>Height:</strong> @Model.Height cm</p>

    <h3>Historical outputs:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Easy:</strong> @Model.EasyCalories kcal/day</li>
        <li><strong>Medium:</strong> @Model.MediumCalories kcal/day</li>
        <li><strong>Hard:</strong> @Model.HardCalories kcal/day</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Body Fat Estimates</h3>
    <p><strong>Current Body Fat:</strong> @(double.IsNaN(Model.CurrentBodyFat) ? "Unavailable" : Model.CurrentBodyFat.ToString("F1") + "%")</p>
    <p><strong>Target Body Fat:</strong> @(double.IsNaN(Model.TargetBodyFat) ? "Unavailable" : Model.TargetBodyFat.ToString("F1") + "%")</p>

}

